Rebased on master, in order to take use of the split-up group element parsing functions (`ge_parse{33,65`, introduced in #1918) in `secp256k1_silentpayments_recipient_prevouts_summary_parse`. Relevant part of the diff:

```diff
@@ -499,12 +496,8 @@ int secp256k1_silentpayments_recipient_prevouts_summary_parse(const secp256k1_co
     ARG_CHECK(input != NULL);
     ARG_CHECK(inputlen == 33 || inputlen == 65);
     /* Since an attacker can send us malicious data that looks like a serialized public key but is not, fail early. */
-    /* TODO: remove manual hybrid pubkey rejection and replace with `secp256k1_ge_parse33` and
-     * `secp256k1_ge_parse65` calls (depending on inputlen) once PR #1918 gets merged */
-    if (inputlen == 65 && input[0] != SECP256K1_TAG_PUBKEY_UNCOMPRESSED) { /* enforce uncompressed format (0x04 prefix) */
-        return 0;
-    }
-    if (!secp256k1_ge_parse(&pk, input, inputlen)) {
+    is_pubkey_valid = (inputlen == 33) ? secp256k1_ge_parse33(&pk, input) : secp256k1_ge_parse65(&pk, input);
+    if (!is_pubkey_valid) {
         return 0;
     }
